# smashcraft#82 box 2, the looks `-dev effects` can't show because it draws no fighter: Mountain
# King a against Mountain King b in a real match. a dashes and runs (footsteps), brakes (its walk
# footstep), hits b's shield (shield spark, struck bubble), hits b (normal spark, damage tint,
# hitlag shake), then grabs, pummels and throws b. Each event is held on its own frame and a
# few frames later. The frames come from `bun scripts/nativeCapture.ts plan` on this file, which
# checks every `#! cue` line; native captures only, as 82-effects.pad.
# A steady walk makes no footstep: only run, brake and turn frames advance the footstep clock
# (smashcraft:ts/src/game/sim/groundMovement.ts), so the walk footstep is the brake's.
#! chat -dev quick hero mountain king
#! cue 30-32 dash footstep: sound=DeepFootstep2 effect=ImpactDust-
#! cue 38-40 run footstep: sound=DeepFootstep2 effect=ImpactDust-
#! cue 61-63 walk footstep: sound=DeepFootstep
#! cue 134-140 shield hit: sound=Defend effect=ImpactShield- recoil=b
#! cue 199-205 normal hit: sound=WoodLightBashFlesh2 effect=StampedeMissileDeath tint=b shake=b
#! cue 255-257 grab: sound=EntanglingRoots effect=ImpactShield-
#! cue 324-330 pummel: sound=Defend effect=StampedeMissileDeath tint=b shake=b
#! cue 349-355 throw: sound=BlinkTarget effect=BlinkTarget
# a dashes, runs and brakes.
30 a stick 1 0
30 a capture
32 a capture
38 a capture
40 a capture
44 a stick 0 0
61 a capture
63 a capture
# a walks up; b shields; a's jab strikes the shield.
70 a stick 0.3 0
88 a stick 0 0
120 b shield 1
130 a tap A 2
134 a capture
136 a capture
140 a capture
# b drops its shield; a walks up and jabs b.
170 b shield 0
172 a stick 0.3 0
190 a stick 0 0
195 a tap A 2
199 a capture
201 a capture
205 a capture
# a walks up and grabs b, pummels once (it connects 60 frames later) and throws b forward.
212 a stick 0.4 0
240 a stick 0 0
248 a tap RB 2
255 a capture
257 a capture
265 a tap A 2
300 a stick 1 0
302 a stick 0 0
324 a capture
326 a capture
330 a capture
349 a capture
351 a capture
355 a capture
